+
+## Revision attempts
+
+After a rejection the teacher may revise its own entry instead of starting over (`teacher/revision.py`,
+`author_revision`). It receives only its previous annotation, that attempt's tool call/result records and a
+pointer-only coverage request, on the byte-identical packet. Imported records are saved in the new run's
+`prior-evidence.json` under `prior:<first 16 hex of the source transcript SHA-256>:<original id>`; the new
+`raw-transcript.json` holds only calls the new session made. Validators merge the two ledgers through the
+`prior` argument of `assemble_draft` and `verify_final`; fresh runs pass nothing and behave as before. One
+revision per rejected attempt is reserved under `.teacher/admin/revisions/`. A revision is always full review.
+In a prepared spec a revision is a `forward` retry with a `revision` object naming `revision_of_run` and the
+coverage `path` and `sha256`.
